  "answer": "Yes, TX-0401 can be disputed under two of the reason codes. I have not opened anything yet.\n\n- **duplicate_charge: eligible.** The deadline is **2026-09-18**, three days from today (2026-09-15).\n- **fraud_card_not_present: eligible.** The deadline is **2026-11-17**.\n- **unauthorized_debit: not eligible.** Its 56-day window closed on 2026-09-14, so this code can no longer be used for this transaction.\n\nWhich code fits depends on what happened. Duplicate charge applies if you were billed twice for one purchase, which TX-0402 may be. Fraud (card not present) applies if your card details were used without your permission. If you tell me which applies, I will confirm before opening the dispute, since it cannot be reversed. If the duplicate-charge deadline matters to you, that is the more urgent option.",
